\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- Banking & Finance: \uc2 Chevron\uc2 's Australia Labor Dispute Flares Up\b0\par\par\uc2 By David Winning \par \uc2 367 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B10\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY -- Workers at two natural-gas facilities operated by \uc2 Chevron\uc2  in Australia have voted to restart industrial action, reigniting a dispute that has rattled global energy markets.\par \par \uc2 The Offshore Alliance, a partnership between two local unions, said the decision was taken at mass meetings of members on Thursday and Friday.\par \par \uc2 It alleged \uc2 Chevron\uc2  had attempted to walk back on an agreement recommended by Australia's workplace arbiter around two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 Australia rivals Qatar as the world's largest exporter of liquefied natural gas. \uc2 Chevron\uc2 's Gorgon and Wheatstone liquefied-natural-gas facilities in Australia, at the center of the labor dispute, account for roughly 7% of global supply.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say disruptions to production from the sites could result in more competition for spot LNG cargoes, with some shipments typically destined for Europe -- including from the U.S. -- likely to be diverted to Asia. European countries have become more reliant on the supercooled fuel since Russia cut off most of the gas it used to pump to the continent.\par \par \uc2 Benchmark European natural-gas prices gained slightly more than 2% in Friday morning trading in London.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for \uc2 Chevron\uc2  in Australia said the company was continuing to work with all parties to finalize the agreements.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Chevron\uc2  workers initially began industrial action on Sept. 8 after negotiations with the U.S. energy company didn't conclude with an agreement on issues such as pay. Within days, \uc2 Chevron\uc2  asked Australia's \uc2 Fair Work Commission\uc2  to intervene to resolve the dispute.\par \par \uc2 On Sept. 21, \uc2 Chevron\uc2  and representatives for the disaffected workers agreed to a deal recommended by the commission, ending the threat of strikes.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Offshore Alliance said it had been working with \uc2 Chevron\uc2  to finalize the drafting of those agreements. However, it said lawyers acting for \uc2 Chevron\uc2  had attempted to walk back some of the clauses that it believed had been settled.\par \par \uc2 "The Offshore Alliance has written to the \uc2 Fair Work Commission\uc2  to apply to have the matter relisted," said Brad Gandy, the alliance's spokesperson. "This ensures workplace issues already agreed to won't be lost due to \uc2 Chevron\uc2 's recent poor behavior."\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020231007eja70000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
