\par\par \b \uc2 UAW Strike Spares Carmakers Financially\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ryan Felton \par \uc2 863 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  strike against Detroit's carmakers, three weeks in, has nearly all the hallmarks of a dug-in labor battle: euphoric worker walkouts, rushed contingency plans, wall-to-wall media coverage and fiery rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 The one thing missing -- at least so far -- is much financial pain, on either side.\par \par \uc2 About 25,000 workers are picketing at \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2  and Chrysler-parent \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  facilities across the Midwest, or about 17% of the companies' unionized workers. \uc2 UAW\uc2  President Shawn Fain is expected to disclose whether there are plans for additional walkouts Friday, in what is becoming a weekly ritual of widening actions.\par \par \uc2 Negotiations continued this week between the union and the three companies on new four-year contracts. \uc2 GM\uc2  confirmed Thursday that it made a recent counteroffer to the union, declining to provide details. Fain is scheduled to provide an update on the talks Friday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The union's gradually unfolding pop-up strikes -- which resemble tactics deployed by the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants\uc2  in the 1990s -- are meant to keep the companies off balance through the element of surprise. It is also aimed at maximizing worker enthusiasm. Union members have gathered while on the job to watch Fain's livestreams to find out if their facility is next to walk out.\par \par \uc2 The union is applying pressure unevenly across the automakers, sparing one company in a given week while turning up the heat on the other two, a tactic intended to pit the companies against one another and reward progress at the bargaining table. Another advantage: It has kept a sizable majority of \uc2 UAW\uc2  members on the job, conserving the fund used to compensate striking workers.\par \par \uc2 Still, the decision to forgo the all-in strike that many industry observers had expected has so far considerably softened the disruption to the companies' factory footprints and bottom lines.\par \par \uc2 For example, when all of \uc2 GM\uc2 's factory workers walked off the job in 2019, the company lost an estimated $1 billion over the first two weeks. Its losses during roughly the first two weeks of the latest strike were about $200 million, a company spokesman said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The five factories on strike across \uc2 GM\uc2 , Ford and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  accounted for about 16% of the vehicles produced in North America by the three companies this year through August, data from Wards Intelligence showed.\par \par \uc2 So far, the plants where the companies' full-size pickup trucks and large SUVs are made -- their most-profitable vehicles -- remain humming.\par \par \uc2 "It's creating a lot of headlines," said \uc2 Colin Langan\uc2 , a \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  analyst. "Financially, it's not very impactful at all."\par \par \uc2 Each automaker has complained that union leaders aren't serious about getting a deal done and are trying to drag out the strike. Last month, they cited purported private messages posted by the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's communications director in which he references keeping the companies "wounded for months" and seeking to do reputational damage to them.\par \par \uc2 "It's clear that there is no real intent to get to an agreement," \uc2 GM\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Mary Barra\uc2  said Friday, after the union staged a walkout at the company's SUV plant in Lansing, Mich.\par \par \uc2 Wages have been a focal point in the talks. The companies have made proposals of roughly 20% wage increases over four years, while the union had been pressing for an increase in the mid-30% range.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  also is demanding cost-of-living adjustments, which it has said \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and Ford have since agreed to, along with better retirement benefits and pensions.\par \par \uc2 The relatively tame financial damage so far is in line with the strategy Fain articulated from the outset, analysts said. He has vowed to gradually turn up the heat on companies that don't move closer to the union's demands.\par \par \uc2 "Fain is still throwing softballs," said Warren Browne, an automotive consultant and retired \uc2 GM\uc2  executive. "I think hardballs will come the longer the strike lasts."\par \par \uc2 Disruption from the limited strike has rippled out to other aspects of the companies' businesses.\par \par \uc2 More than 6,000 workers at the three companies and at outside suppliers have been put on temporary layoff because of knock-on effects from certain operations going down from the strike.\par \par \uc2 Last week, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  was subject to the whipsaw effect of the union's strike strategy.\par \par \uc2 On Friday morning last week, Fain spared \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  from further strikes, while calling further walkouts at \uc2 GM\uc2  and Ford. But \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  executives didn't have time to celebrate, as they rushed to contain fallout from the prior week's labor action.\par \par \uc2 Later that day, the company's top North American executive told employees in an email that "passionate volunteers" were immediately needed to work shifts at two Michigan parts-distribution sites that had gone on strike the previous week.\par \par \uc2 Employees were being asked to meet early the next morning, a Saturday, to board charter buses to the facilities. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Both \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  have scrambled to find white-collar staff to work shifts at 38 parts depots that went on strike in the second wave announced by the \uc2 UAW\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Nora Eckert contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020231006eja60003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
