\par\par \b \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  CEO Tavares Has Success With \uc2 UAW\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ryan Felton \par \uc2 849 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Carlos Tavares\uc2 , chief executive of Chrysler parent \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , was off to a rocky start in his first-ever contract talks with the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Soon after negotiations began in July, \uc2 UAW\uc2  President Shawn Fain criticized Tavares for failing to show up at an early bargaining round. A few weeks later, Fain publicly threw \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 's initial offer in a trash can. Recently, union leaders blasted the company for its response to the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's proposals around job security and profit sharing.\par \par \uc2 But Friday brought a twist: \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  delivered a last-minute offer that showed significant progress toward some key \uc2 UAW\uc2  demands, Fain said. The union spared \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  from further strike actions -- for now -- while conducting more walkouts at \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That decision was a rare reprieve from the fraying tensions in Detroit, as the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's strike against the three automakers enters its third week. About 25,000 factory workers are off the job as the rhetoric from both sides sharpens.\par \par \uc2 Across all three automakers, wage increases are a primary issue. The companies recently had on the table offers of 20% wage hikes over four years, while the union has been pressing for a bump at least in the mid-30% range. Other demands include cost-of-living increases and higher pay for newer workers.\par \par \uc2 Tavares, a Portuguese native, made his mark by turning around money-losing auto manufacturers in France and Germany, in part by coaxing voluntary job cuts and concessions from Europe's tough union heads. As the three automakers face pressure from the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's widening strike, Tavares's labor-relations chops are being put to the test.\par \par \uc2 "I can't imagine him and Shawn in the same room going up against each other," said \uc2 Ron Harbour\uc2 , an automotive consultant and analyst. "Shawn will have met his match."\par \par \uc2 For decades, Chrysler -- the predecessor of \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 's North American operations -- was the smallest and least profitable of the three Detroit car companies and most dependent on the U.S. to fuel its bottom line. Now, as the more global and more profitable \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , those dynamics have flipped.\par \par \uc2 Italy's \uc2 Fiat\uc2  effectively took control of Chrysler as the American automaker climbed out of its 2009 bankruptcy and fully acquired the company in 2014. In January 2021, \uc2 Fiat Chrysler\uc2  merged with France's \uc2 PSA Group\uc2 , then led by Tavares, creating \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  has emerged as the world's fourth-largest car company by sales, ahead of \uc2 GM\uc2  and Ford. Sales of rugged Jeep SUVs and brawny Ram pickup trucks in the U.S. are a major profit generator.\par \par \uc2 But the company is more diverse than its two rivals, which generate nearly all of their profits in North America. It has established European brands, such as \uc2 Peugeot\uc2  and \uc2 Opel\uc2 , and a strong presence in South America.\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 's superior profitability in North America has left it open to Fain's criticism and strengthens the union's bargaining leverage, analysts say. The company's operating-profit margin for the region in 2022 was 16.4%, compared with 10.1% for \uc2 GM\uc2  and 8.4% for Ford.\par \par \uc2 An engineer by training, Tavares started his career in 1981 as a test-track driver at France's \uc2 Renault\uc2 , where he rose through the ranks before becoming an executive at \uc2 Nissan Motor\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After taking over \uc2 PSA\uc2  in 2014, Tavares developed a reputation for maintaining sharp metrics to track progress and being hyperfocused on cost -- he has been known to fly budget airlines instead of private jets used by many CEOs.\par \par \uc2 "He's tough but sensible," said \uc2 Carla Bailo\uc2 , who worked with Tavares during his time at \uc2 Nissan\uc2 . She said the CEO "has clear objectives in what a win means for him and the company. He will listen, though, to a compelling argument."\par \par \uc2 Tavares operates the company with a focus on efficiency, and that cost management is key to sustaining \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  over time, the company said.\par \par \uc2 "We only ask for a fair competition with the [foreign] transplants and the newcomers on the U.S. market," the company said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 PSA\uc2  acquired \uc2 Opel\uc2  from \uc2 GM\uc2  in 2017, analysts figured Tavares faced a battle to turn it around, in part because they expected powerful European labor unions would block cost-cutting moves. Nonetheless, he pressed unions to accept job cuts to stabilize \uc2 Opel\uc2 's bottom line, quickly swinging it to a profit.\par \par \uc2 Now, Tavares's cost-conscious style has taken on new urgency amid the industry's transition to electric vehicles. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  is spending $35 billion through 2025 as part of its effort to make the leap to EVs.\par \par \uc2 "If we stop working on cost, in this industry you go from hero to zero," Tavares told reporters in January.\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  has the smallest \uc2 UAW\uc2  workforce of the three companies, with about 43,000 represented employees, compared with \uc2 GM\uc2 's 46,000 and Ford's 57,000. It also has more leverage than \uc2 GM\uc2  and Ford to consider shifting some factory work to Canada and Mexico, said \uc2 Sam Fiorani\uc2 , an analyst with AutoForecast Solutions.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020231002eja200034\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
