\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. Cites Racial Hostility At Tesla Factory --- \uc2 EEOC\uc2  says Black employees face harassment, slurs at California workplace\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Elliott \par \uc2 724 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 September 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  was accused of subjecting Black employees at its California auto-assembly plant to racial harassment and a hostile work environment in a federal lawsuit filed Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission\uc2  also alleged that \uc2 Tesla\uc2  unlawfully retaliated against Black employees and engaged in discriminatory conduct since at least 2015.\par \par \uc2 The move turns the spotlight back on \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's Fremont, Calif., factory, which in recent years has been the subject of allegations of racial harassment and discrimination among workers on the factory floor.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EEOC\uc2 's claims of widespread racial misconduct at the plant echo those made in a lawsuit filed last year by a California civil rights agency that claimed \uc2 Tesla\uc2  ignored years of complaints from Black factory workers.\par \par \uc2 "The racial misconduct was frequent, ongoing, inappropriate, unwelcome and occurred across all shifts, departments, and positions," the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  said in the lawsuit filed in the Northern District of California. The agency cited the use of racial slurs, racist epithets and race-based stereotyping.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has said it "strongly opposes all forms of discrimination and harassment" and has a track record of disciplining and terminating employees who use racial slurs and engage in other forms of misconduct.\par \par \uc2 More than 20,000 people work at the Fremont factory, where \uc2 Tesla\uc2  manufactures its top-selling electric vehicles -- the Model Y crossover and Model 3 sedan -- as well as its luxury EVs.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EEOC\uc2  said it sought to settle with \uc2 Tesla\uc2  before filing its lawsuit and was unable to reach an agreement. In the past, Chief Executive \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has demonstrated a willingness to see legal disputes through to trial.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  rose 2.4% Thursday to $246.38.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit claims \uc2 Tesla\uc2  failed to investigate complaints or adopt policies to ensure temporary workers didn't harass their colleagues. The company also is accused of firing Black employees after they reported or opposed racial harassment.\par \par \uc2 One Black worker saw death threats and racist graffiti in the bathroom, the lawsuit said.\par \par \uc2 Many of \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's factory workers are contractors employed through staffing agencies, and the company previously has sought to distance itself from the behavior and experiences of those workers.\par \par \uc2 In 2021, a jury found \uc2 Tesla\uc2  liable for subjecting a Black former elevator operator, who was employed through a staffing agency, to a racially hostile work environment and failing to prevent racial harassment. A separate jury ordered \uc2 Tesla\uc2  to pay more than $3 million in damages.\par \par \uc2 The California agency's lawsuit is pending. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has alleged the department violated state rules in bringing the suit.\par \par \uc2 Cases brought by the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  can lead to financial penalties. For example, Ford agreed in 2017 to pay up to about $10 million to settle claims of racial and sexual harassment, as well as retaliation, involving employees at two Chicago-area plants.\par \par \uc2 The federal agency also has asked the court to order \uc2 Tesla\uc2  to adopt policies aimed at ensuring equal employment opportunities for Black workers.\par \par \uc2 Such labor issues can draw the attention of unions. Several years ago, workers at Fremont sought to organize with the help of the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  took steps to hinder that effort in violation of U.S. labor law, the National Labor Relation Relations Board has ruled. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has appealed and denies wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  is on strike at \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2  and Chrysler parent \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , after contract negotiations with the automakers failed to produce new labor contracts.\par \par \uc2 Musk's companies are facing federal scrutiny on several fronts, including from the Justice Department.\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors based in Manhattan are investigating personal benefits that \uc2 Tesla\uc2  might have provided Musk since 2017 as part of a criminal probe that deals with issues including a proposed house for the CEO, The Wall Street Journal has reported.\par \par \uc2 As of last year, federal prosecutors in Washington and San Francisco were investigating whether the carmaker misled consumers and investors about how its advanced driver-assistance system known as Autopilot performed.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the Justice Department sued Musk's rocket company, \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , last month, alleging the company discriminated against refugees by discouraging them from applying for jobs and refusing to hire them. \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  has sought to block the DOJ's lawsuit, calling it unconstitutional, while denying it discriminated against job seekers.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230929ej9t0006i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
