\par\par \b \uc2 Ford Reaches Deal With Canada Union\b0\par\par\uc2 By Vipal Monga and Nora Eckert \par \uc2 312 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2  reached a new tentative labor deal late Tuesday with Canadian labor \uc2 union Unifor\uc2 , avoiding what could have been a second strike at the automaker's operations in less than a week.\par \par \uc2 Contract talks with Unifor have been running parallel to those in the U.S. with the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2 , an unusual overlap that has put pressure on Ford and its two Detroit rivals -- \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and Chrysler parent \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  -- with two unions simultaneously pressing for more in pay and benefits.\par \par \uc2 Unifor and the company didn't disclose details of the tentative agreement, which covers about 5,600 members at Ford's Canadian facilities. The union said it would present details to members in meetings ahead of a ratification vote.\par \par \uc2 Unifor, which is separate from the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , represents roughly 18,000 workers at \uc2 GM\uc2 , Ford and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  in Canada.\par \par \uc2 The union had said it was pressing Ford for improved pensions, higher wages, and some form of support to protect workers as the company transitions to making electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 Unlike in the U.S., where the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has taken an unorthodox approach to talks, Unifor has gone a more traditional route by targeting one automaker to reach a deal with first, with the intention of using that agreement as a template for the other two.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian union extended its contracts at \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  to continue bargaining with those two and will likely turn to one of them next, a union spokeswoman said Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 "This agreement makes the kind of gains our members need today and adds greater financial security for the future," said Unifor Ford Master Bargaining Chair John D'Agnolo.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, negotiations between the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and the three Detroit automakers covering about 146,000 U.S. workers have continued this week with no resolution.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230920ej9k0006k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
