\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- Chevron Australian Plants Face Labor Strife\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rhiannon Hoyle \par \uc2 421 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ADELAIDE, Australia -- Workers at two natural-gas plants run by \uc2 Chevron\uc2  in Australia began industrial action Friday, intensifying a dispute that has rattled global gas markets.\par \par \uc2 A week of talks between \uc2 Chevron\uc2  and staff at its Gorgon and Wheatstone liquefied-natural-gas facilities had failed to produce an agreement on issues such as pay.\par \par \uc2 Offshore Alliance, a partnership of two local unions, said the action would include work bans and short stoppages ahead of a two-week walkout starting Sept. 14, the group said.\par \par \uc2 Chevron\uc2  said it had negotiated in good faith but couldn't accept the demands sought by representatives of the around 500 workers.\par \par \uc2 Gas markets have been jittery about the prospect of strike action in recent months, as Australia rivals Qatar as the world's largest exporter of liquefied natural gas, and the \uc2 Chevron\uc2  facilities are among Australia's largest. They account for about 7% of global LNG supply, according to Wood Mackenzie, a commodities research and consulting firm.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say disruptions to production from the sites could result in more competition for spot LNG cargoes, with some shipments typically destined for Europe -- including from the U.S. -- likely to be diverted to Asia. European countries have become more reliant on the supercooled fuel since Russia cut off most of the gas it used to pump to the continent.\par \par \uc2 Natural-gas prices in Europe were up nearly 10% Friday at just under 36 euros, or $38.65, a megawatt hour. Still, analysts say large stockpiles of gas that Europe has accumulated before demand rises over winter should prevent a repeat of the haywire price moves that hobbled some industries last year.\par \par \uc2 Offshore Alliance had signaled industrial action was likely in a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post earlier Friday, saying it had rebuffed \uc2 Chevron\uc2 , which it said had sought special concessions. Some operations at the \uc2 Chevron\uc2  facilities would be shut down if there weren't enough qualified personnel available during work stoppages, but a plant at Wheatstone supplying the local market with gas wouldn't be affected by the action, the group said.\par \par \uc2 "After five days \uc2 Chevron\uc2  has barely budged," Offshore Alliance spokesman Brad Gandy said of negotiations that began Monday.\par \par \uc2 Offshore Alliance said it wants an agreement that aligns with those in place at energy companies including \uc2 Shell\uc2  and Japan's \uc2 Inpex\uc2 . Last month, the group reached a preliminary deal with \uc2 Woodside Energy\uc2  to avert possible strike action at three offshore LNG platforms in Australia.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Joe Wallace contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230909ej990000q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
