\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: Las Vegas Hotel Staff to Vote on Strike Approval\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ginger Adams Otis \par \uc2 257 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Unions for Las Vegas Strip workers have set a date for a citywide strike vote later this month that, if approved, could lead to more than 50,000 housekeepers, bartenders and other staff walking off the job.\par \par \uc2 Members of the Culinary and Bartenders Unions will cast ballots on Sept. 26. A majority vote would authorize a potential future strike.\par \par \uc2 Among other issues, workers want lighter workloads and an increase in on-the-job security protection, the unions said. They are also bargaining for a wage increase.\par \par \uc2 A majority of the workers are employed in the hotels, casinos and restaurants on the Las Vegas Strip or in downtown Las Vegas.\par \par \uc2 The affected properties include casino-resorts handled or owned by \uc2 Caesars Entertainment\uc2 , \uc2 Wynn Resorts\uc2 , and \uc2 MGM Resorts International\uc2  as well as hotels that don't have on-site gambling.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Wynn Resorts\uc2  spokesman declined to comment on the vote. Requests for comment to other hotels weren't returned.\par \par \uc2 The Culinary Union, the largest labor union in Nevada, and the Bartenders Union, which together represent the 53,000 workers whose contracts are up for negotiation, said they would continue to bargain with hotel and casino companies ahead of the strike vote.\par \par \uc2 The Culinary Union has called a strike vote as part of contract talks in the past, most recently in 2018. That year a strike was authorized by the membership, but a walkout was avoided with a five-year contract that expires this year.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230908ej980003k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
