\par\par \b \uc2 Strike Dims Warner Profit Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 By Will Feuer \par \uc2 264 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 September 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Warner Bros. Discovery\uc2  cut its full-year adjusted earnings outlook as the Hollywood labor strikes drag on longer than the entertainment conglomerate expected.\par \par \uc2 The parent company of CNN, \uc2 HBO\uc2  and other networks had hoped the strikes would be resolved by early September. \uc2 Warner Bros\uc2 . said Tuesday in a securities filing that it can't predict when the strikes will end, and it expects the financial fallout to affect the company through year-end.\par \par \uc2 Warner Bros\uc2 . said it is now targeting full-year adjusted earnings, before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization, of $10.5 billion to $11 billion, down by $500 million on both the lower and upper bounds from guidance issued last month.\par \par \uc2 The company said the hit is mostly a result of the strikes.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the company also raised its free-cash-flow outlook for the year to at least $5 billion, driven in part by the strong performance of the "Barbie" movie.\par \par \uc2 Matthew Thornton, an analyst at investment bank \uc2 Truist\uc2 , said the change to full-year guidance was unsurprising given the state of the strikes.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Warner Bros\uc2 . rose 0.7% Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The Writers Guild of America and \uc2 Screen Actors Guild\uc2  have been striking since May and July, respectively. If a deal isn't reached soon, the 2023-2024 television season and many high-profile movies are likely to be delayed or scrapped altogether.\par \par \uc2 A coalition representing Hollywood studios and streaming services have offered concessions to the WGA, but the union has said the offers fall short of their expectations.\par \par \uc2 Document 